#!/usr/bin/env perl
use 5.014;
use strict;
use warnings;

use Game::Floppy::Terminal;

our $VERSION = '0.10';

exit Game::Floppy::Terminal->run(@ARGV);

__END__

=head1 NAME

floppy - a one-button bird through a field of tubes, in a terminal or a window

=head1 SYNOPSIS

    floppy                     # play, the view fitted to the window
    floppy --watch --level 3   # watch the bot
    floppy --raylib            # a window, when Raylib::FFI is installed
    floppy --help

=head1 DESCRIPTION

Space, up, Enter, w or k flap; p pauses; q quits; after a death, space plays
again. The bird falls, a flap lifts it, and it dies on a tube, on the ground
or off the top. Passing a tube scores 100.

The keys need L<Term::ReadKey>. Without it the game says so and exits 2;
C<--watch> works anywhere.

=head1 EXIT STATUS

0 when a game ended or was quit; 2 for a bad option, or a game that could not
start.

=head1 SEE ALSO

L<Game::Floppy::Terminal>, which this program is two lines over.

